# Accepted trivy config findings (HIGH/CRITICAL). Each entry is a design choice documented in ARCHITECTURE.md/README.md;
# remove the entry when the choice changes. Used by the CI trivy step (trivyignores) and locally:
#   trivy config --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignorefile .trivyignore .

# SNS topics of app data use the AWS-managed key (alias/aws/sns) when no kms_key_arn is given (modules/event-topic).
AVD-AWS-0136

# SQS queues of app data use SSE-SQS (AWS-managed) when no kms_key_arn is given (modules/messaging-queue).
AVD-AWS-0135

# S3 app buckets use SSE-S3 (AWS-managed) when no kms_key_arn is given (modules/app-bucket).
AVD-AWS-0132

# EKS node security group egress 0.0.0.0/0 (community eks module): nodes pull images and call AWS APIs through
# the NAT because there are no VPC endpoints yet (known gap in README.md).
AVD-AWS-0104
